                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d680d9b6-dd79-3ff3-a7ac-4b61c851599e",
                        "entry_id": "edf87e4b-2701-3b0e-a0c8-5fd50bd48f17",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A plot within a story, subsidiary to the main plot."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0008b201-2a5b-40b3-9f4d-78dab5e52cef",
                                "sense_id": "d680d9b6-dd79-3ff3-a7ac-4b61c851599e",
                                "text": "1978, R.B. Lee & R. Misiorowski, Script Models: A Handbook for the Media Writer,\nSubplot, a story line enclosed within the principal story to provide relief from the main plot's tension, add character dimension, etc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d50c7b45-6ebe-4bea-a665-a63de2549f98",
                                "sense_id": "d680d9b6-dd79-3ff3-a7ac-4b61c851599e",
                                "text": "Structurally, the two most variant scenes (outside of Scene ii) are Scenes 3 and 4 in which the compiler works out the variant subplot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a7feb72-aadf-4164-ae85-5a9fd119a6f3",
                                "sense_id": "d680d9b6-dd79-3ff3-a7ac-4b61c851599e",
                                "text": "In a sense, Superman's romance with Lois Lane was a subplot and [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a914f09-abb1-4c7e-93b7-c0f43ef28793",
                                "sense_id": "d680d9b6-dd79-3ff3-a7ac-4b61c851599e",
                                "text": "2001, Nancy Arbuthnot Johnson, Vic Neufield, Forging Links for Health Research,\nBut this story has a subplot — a subplot about fairness and how people have divergent levels of access to knowledge and resources."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6c071c42-30dc-3f1a-afa5-1c511b9d4015",
                        "entry_id": "edf87e4b-2701-3b0e-a0c8-5fd50bd48f17",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A subdivision of a plot of land, especially one used for an agricultural experiment."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2d6c29c-e258-47cf-9245-e85304069fad",
                                "sense_id": "6c071c42-30dc-3f1a-afa5-1c511b9d4015",
                                "text": "[...] on sixteen 8/10-acre plots (12.8 acres) well distributed over the area. [...] A 1/160-acre subplot was established in a randomly chosen corner of each [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "12ccbf82-428d-44b2-97ed-84cd032c1a37",
                                "sense_id": "6c071c42-30dc-3f1a-afa5-1c511b9d4015",
                                "text": "1999, E. K. Sadanandan Nambiar, Christian Cossalter, Site Management and Productivity in Tropical Plantation Forest,\nThere are 72 trees in each plot (6x12) and 36 trees in each subplot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68bbace4-5d23-49af-8e7e-b7966368e2ab",
                                "sense_id": "6c071c42-30dc-3f1a-afa5-1c511b9d4015",
                                "text": "2002, M. Boya Edwards, Proceedings for the Eight Biennial Southern Silvicultural Research Conference,\nHardwood and shrub stems (besides gallberry) were counted by species and measured for total height (if greater than 2 ft) on 3 strip plots per subplot that were 0.01 acre […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
